      "value": "@{60592db8826873531cae715d|full_name}: Crypto in general has been an environmental catastrophe. If they plan to be carbon neutral in 2030, that's great, come back in 2030. Until then, no thanks. The ends don't justify the means. I don't care that Bitcoin is worse -- I'd prefer that didn't exist either. Yes I've read the link in your post. No, it's not good enough for the questionable amount of value it provides in anything even approaching the near term.\nThere's a reason this canny has had precisely zero signatures aside from your own in the 17 hours it's been up at this point. Outside the crypto echo-chamber, most people aren't happy with the state of things if they're informed enough to have an opinion at all. The fact that you confidently declare 'this is the future of gaming' shows how firmly embedded in said echo-chamber you are. \nCould it be *a* future? Sure. It's not worth much right now though, I doubt that's going to change much in the next decade, and it could be completely supplanted by something else in the mean time. VRChat needs to think about surviving the next few years right now, not what their position will be in 2031. Their last round of VC investment was series C, and their focus needs to be on growing their platform as much as possible right now. A more conventional storefront integration would do a better job of raising capital toward that end at the moment than something like Enjin, and be a lot more straight forward to implement as it's a very well-tracted problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
