  "details": "Short intro: I am not hired by Enjin, I am just a dedicated 10+ years members of the Enjin network with 50+ hours in VRChat and have thought of this idea and would like to share it.\nI am aware avatars are a big part of VRChat and is a useful way for people to communicate, I am also aware VRChat is looking for ways to commercialise its F2P game for example \"VRChat Plus\".\nI believe the VRChat should take a serious step towards adapting its game onto the blockchain with the help of Enjin (because they make it so easy and are pretty much the gaming giant for blockchain right now!) I believe Enjin would definitely offer partnership with VRChat if this were to happen.\nImagine a VRChat marketplace (EnjinX) where players can purchase cosmetics (animations, NFT avatars etc) which the player owns completely since it's stored on the blockchain. This blockchain asset then can also be used with OTHER GAMES since it would be stored in your Enjin wallet.\nI encourage the VRChat team to really look into this and research Enjin, I am just a devoted community member and not affiliated with Enjin.\n \nThis is the future of gaming.\nWould be happy to answer any questions!",
